※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4365

※ **`⎕at` makes a function only of the system's convention.**  An address is
※ one word, where code is; a function of the language's own convention is three
※ words, two of them about what it brought in, which no address says.

let std := ⎕import("std")

@[startup]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    let f: fn(u64) → u64 = ⎕at(4096u64, ⌜fn(u64) → u64⌝)
    if f(2u64) = 6u64: 0u6 else: 1u6
